WEBVTT

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.720
<b>Yo, yo, yonaka ni bakko suru chimi mouryou</b>

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:27.720
<i>Yo, yo, at midnight evil spirits stalk</i>

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.760
<b>Marude ikaino ichimi routou</b>

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.760
<i>As if they're from another world</i>

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.010
<b>Mitai na rhymer rhyme shini toujou</b>

00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:32.010
<i>Come to rhyme rhymes</i>

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.180
<b>Kikoetarou? Yamini hibiku oto</b>

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:34.180
<i>Can you hear them? The sounds resonating from the darkness</i>

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.520
<b>Bibitte kyomi nai furi shiyouto</b>

00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:36.520
<i>Scared senseless, but you pretend not to be interested</i>

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.480
<b>Koukishin wa hini hini jyoushou</b>

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.480
<i>Your curiosity grows day by day</i>

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.770
<b>Nara check shini ikou, here we, here we go ya'll!</b>

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.770
<i>So let's go check them out, here we, here we go ya'll</i>

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:42.980
<b>Ayashi ayaushi shima no chimi mouryou</b>

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:42.980
<i>The mysterious and dangerous evil spirits</i>

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:44.650
<b>Tabun jigoku wa manpai</b>

00:00:43.190 --> 00:00:44.650
<i>Hell is probably full with evil spirits</i>

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.940
<b>Afure dashita renchuu ga dantai de retsu wo nashite</b>

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.940
<i>Those that can't get in march in a line</i>

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.150
<b>Kono yo ni stand-by</b>

00:00:48.030 --> 00:00:49.150
<i>Waiting on stand-by in this world</i>

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.360
<b>Yatsura no bun basho ga mazu tannai</b>

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.360
<i>There aren't any spaces left for them</i>

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:53.620
<b>Dooride kisetsu towazu atsui hazu</b>

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:53.620
<i>No wonder, no matter what the season is, it's always hot</i>

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:56.240
<b>Aete heat up sasu ikatsui verse wo</b>

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:56.240
<i>Purposely heating you up with hot verses</i>

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.950
<b>Kamashite ase kakasuzo</b>

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.950
<i>That make you sweat</i>

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.710
<b>Douse yakedaro kikasena gasshou wo yo!</b>

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.710
<i>You might as well let us hear you all sing!</i>

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:02.790
<b>HA! Koitsuwa marude kajiba</b>

00:01:00.830 --> 00:01:02.790
<i>HA! It's just like a scene of a fire</i>

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.170
<b>Sugee nekki tamacchimau shimaguni</b>

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.170
<i>The excitement in the air heats up this island country</i>

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.300
<b>DANGER! Masu masu agacchimau COME ON!</b>

00:01:05.250 --> 00:01:07.300
<i>DANGER! The tension keeps building COME ON!</i>

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.550
<b>(Kono Jipangu mouchoi de panku!)</b>

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.550
<i>(This Japan is about to explode!)</i>

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.680
<b>HA! Koitsuwa marude kajiba</b>

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.680
<i>HA! It's just like a scene of a fire</i>

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.970
<b>Sugee nekki tamacchimau shimaguni</b>

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.970
<i>The excitement in the air heats up this island country</i>

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.180
<b>DANGER! Masu masu agacchimau COME ON!</b>

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:16.180
<i>DANGER! The tension keeps building COME ON!</i>

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.390
<b>(Kono Jipangu mouchoi de panku!)</b>

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:18.390
<i>(This Japan is about to explode!)</i>

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:23.770
It is said that Oiwa
of Tokaido Yotsuya Kaidan

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:27.900
cursed the houses of Ito and
Tamiya until neither had

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:29.940
any remaining descendants.

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:33.700
However, the tradition that
is observed at Oiwa's shrine

00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:36.660
differs greatly from the play itself.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:39.580
The wife of Tamiya lemon, Oiwa,

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:42.170
was well known
for being a hard worker,

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:46.420
and she prayed daily at the shrine
on her family's estate.

00:01:46.630 --> 00:01:48.550
Impressed by her behaviour,

00:01:48.630 --> 00:01:51.050
neighbors followed her example,

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:53.130
praying here to this very day.

00:01:54.260 --> 00:01:57.260
The real Oiwa that actually existed

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:59.180
was the model
of a virtuous woman.

00:01:59.220 --> 00:02:02.350
Or perhaps,
betrayed by her husband,

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:06.690
she had in death become a vengeful
ghost that cursed others.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.990
I was Tsuruya Nanboku the Fourth.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.780
Let us continue the story
of Tokaido Yotsuya Kaidan.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:19.580
I curse you, lemon!

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:25.080
Act Three

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:32.300
Due to Oiwa's curse,
the House of Ito was ruined.

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:53.570
No eels, huh?

00:02:53.650 --> 00:02:54.950
Huh? What's this?

00:02:56.110 --> 00:02:57.200
A comb?

00:02:57.530 --> 00:03:00.910
Well, I guess it wasn't
a complete waste after all.

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:05.460
Honestly, when did things
become so troublesome?

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:09.960
lemon,

00:03:10.130 --> 00:03:12.420
I'm going to pretend
that you're dead.

00:03:12.460 --> 00:03:15.050
I'm sorry I've been a cause
for such worry.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.010
Look.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:19.100
I've even prepared a wooden epitaph
to mark your passing.

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:24.930
It's a strange feeling to look
at one's own epitaph.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.310
Well, take care of yourself.

00:03:36.990 --> 00:03:38.160
Master Tamiya.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:40.070
Naosuke?

00:03:40.490 --> 00:03:41.950
It's been a long time.

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.450
I heard what happened.

00:03:43.490 --> 00:03:45.750
Sounds like you outdid
yourself this time.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:49.290
Thought so.
You really are a wicked one.

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:52.670
You can chop off my head,
I'll keep coming back.

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:04.140
There was no doubt
lemon was an evil man,

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:06.520
having killed his father-in-law,
Oiwa's father,

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:08.520
as well as his servant Kohei.

00:04:08.850 --> 00:04:09.730
However,

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:13.190
it was Ito Kihei who had
given Oiwa the poison.

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:17.070
lemon had merely acted
as an accomplice.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:20.570
Looks like it's going to rain.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.080
I'm off. Nice talking with you.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:02.030
The Tamiya bloodline

00:05:04.530 --> 00:05:07.370
and the Ito bloodline
shall be slain.

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:09.750
Damn you!

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:11.870
I curse you!

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:15.000
Go to the nether world!

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:21.260
Give me the medicine!

00:05:21.300 --> 00:05:23.050
Is this a curse?!

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:25.930
Damn!

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:29.060
lemon!

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:42.950
Elsewhere, Oiwa's sister Osode

00:05:42.990 --> 00:05:45.990
had yet to realize that the one
who had killed Yomoshichi

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:48.620
was none other than Naosuke.

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:52.750
Fooled by his offer to help
find her fiancé's killer,

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:55.790
they lived together pretending
to be husband and wife.

00:05:56.460 --> 00:06:00.550
Poor Osode was still
unaware of Oiwa's death.

00:06:01.050 --> 00:06:02.090
Osode.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:03.970
Oh, the cloth trader.

00:06:04.760 --> 00:06:08.350
Would you mind washing
this kimono while you're at it?

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:11.310
Where did you get that from?

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:15.310
From a corpse nailed to a door,
found floating down river.

00:06:16.150 --> 00:06:17.690
You got it off a corpse?!

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.150
I'm just joking.

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.240
I'll pick it up later.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:28.160
Got rained out.

00:06:31.120 --> 00:06:32.620
I'm back earlier than planned.

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:35.670
Oh, right. I didn't catch any eels,

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:36.880
but I found this,

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:39.550
and thought it'd
look good on you.

00:06:43.380 --> 00:06:45.470
That comb belongs
to my sister Oiwa!

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:48.010
What?!

00:06:48.180 --> 00:06:50.010
I remember it well.

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:54.600
She showed it to me once,
promising to give it to me one day.

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:56.810
Wait for me!

00:07:01.730 --> 00:07:02.440
Oh, here.

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:03.900
It's beautiful.

00:07:04.450 --> 00:07:05.280
- Let me have it, sister!

00:07:05.280 --> 00:07:06.820
- Let me have it, sister!
- No. No.

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:17.170
Well, you might as well keep it.

00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:20.710
Perhaps if we were blood sisters,

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:22.670
but I'm only her adopted kin.

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:26.340
Take it back tomorrow
to the Yotsuya family.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:36.310
I can't show my face to sister
Oiwa now, living like this.

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:40.110
Why should I return it
for nothing?

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:54.160
Something the matter?

00:08:00.670 --> 00:08:02.380
Must've seen a ghost.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:05.010
It's nothing.

00:08:08.930 --> 00:08:10.180
That's good timing.

00:08:10.220 --> 00:08:11.930
Hey, come this way!

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:13.720
Yes?

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:15.770
Come here a second.

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.600
Sure. Excuse the intrusion.

00:08:19.350 --> 00:08:22.940
Well, if it isn't
Takuetsu from Asakusa.

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:27.360
Yes, it's been a while,
Naosuke and Lady Osode.

00:08:47.590 --> 00:08:48.970
That comb!

00:08:49.010 --> 00:08:51.050
That belongs to Oiwa!
From the Yotsuya family.

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:54.220
What? You know of my sister Oiwa?

00:08:54.310 --> 00:08:55.680
I certainly do.

00:08:56.140 --> 00:09:00.100
I witnessed that whole gruesome
scene with my own eyes.

00:09:00.190 --> 00:09:01.600
Did something happen to her?

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:03.400
Well...

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:06.440
If I die now,

00:09:07.860 --> 00:09:11.530
lemon will be bound in
matrimony to that Oume.

00:09:16.450 --> 00:09:19.330
I will hold a grudge
against you, lemon!

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:24.750
You will never live this down!

00:09:37.220 --> 00:09:40.520
She might as well have
been killed by lemon.

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:44.480
Osode, get a hold of yourself.

00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:49.030
We must avenge Oiwa's death!

00:09:49.110 --> 00:09:51.150
Where has lemon gone?

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:54.240
Actually, I have no idea
where he's gone.

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:56.200
That's all I have to say.

00:09:56.240 --> 00:09:58.450
Now, if you'll excuse me.

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:13.760
As it stands, the only one
that can claim revenge for Oiwa

00:10:13.840 --> 00:10:16.510
is you, Osode.
Just you.

00:10:17.390 --> 00:10:19.390
You're not going to help me?

00:10:19.970 --> 00:10:22.430
Well, we're only pretending
to be married.

00:10:22.520 --> 00:10:25.060
If we were actually married,

00:10:25.150 --> 00:10:27.440
your revenge would
be my revenge.

00:10:32.990 --> 00:10:35.360
What if we were to be married?

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:38.080
Would you help me
avenge her death?

00:10:38.990 --> 00:10:42.200
Only if we share the same bed,
like a real couple.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:45.710
All right. Starting tonight.

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:47.880
That's good to hear.

00:10:47.920 --> 00:10:49.710
So you finally agree.

00:10:53.670 --> 00:10:56.050
You have no idea how long
I've waited for this day.

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:23.450
lemon's mother, Okuma,

00:11:23.540 --> 00:11:25.460
after the House of Asano
was dissolved,

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:29.000
defected to serve under
their adversaries, the House of Kira.

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:33.460
And she became the second wife
of Hotoke Magobei,

00:11:33.550 --> 00:11:35.300
Kobotoke Kohei's father.

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:35.800
- Give me a break!

00:11:35.800 --> 00:11:36.970
- Kohei's son, Jiroukichi
- Give me a break!

00:11:36.970 --> 00:11:39.220
- Kohei's son, Jiroukichi
to whom she had no blood ties,

00:11:39.260 --> 00:11:42.720
was treated very cruelly
every day by Okuma.

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:46.940
Don't tell me this is all
the clams you sold today!

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.690
I'm sorry! I'm sorry!

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:53.690
Get back out there and sell
more clams while it's light out.

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.490
If father were here...

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:58.450
When he comes back...!

00:11:58.820 --> 00:12:01.410
Your father, Kobotoke Kohei,

00:12:01.450 --> 00:12:04.620
died a long time ago
and is never coming back!

00:12:05.620 --> 00:12:08.960
Sell as much as I told you to
or else don't expect any dinner!

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:20.180
What're you doing?
You're scaring me.

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:25.350
The one who killed me is...

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:28.350
Tamiya lemon!

00:12:40.610 --> 00:12:44.490
The man who passed by
Naosuke and Osode's house

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:48.870
was Osode's fiancée, who Naosuke
believed he had murdered.

00:12:51.380 --> 00:12:53.880
It was Sato Yomoshichi.

00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:14.570
Lady Oiwa!

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:26.740
Whose house is this?

00:13:31.170 --> 00:13:32.460
Excuse me.

00:13:32.540 --> 00:13:33.880
Forgive my intrusion.

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:37.550
Something strange happened
outside your house.

00:13:38.210 --> 00:13:39.210
Hello?

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:40.380
Is anyone home?

00:13:41.220 --> 00:13:42.470
Keep it down!

00:13:42.630 --> 00:13:45.010
What's with you barging
into a stranger's house like that?

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:47.390
Who are you, anyway?

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:52.060
It's a ghost!

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:53.940
You're Naosuke!

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:56.190
That voice.

00:13:56.820 --> 00:13:57.900
That voice is...

00:13:57.980 --> 00:13:59.030
It can't be!

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:00.530
Osode!

00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:02.570
Yomoshichi!

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:04.280
You're alive!

00:14:04.990 --> 00:14:06.950
You were alive all this time.

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:13.960
Yes, I'm certainly not a ghost.

00:14:14.540 --> 00:14:18.130
Weren't you killed in an abandoned
paddy in Asakusa?

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:22.380
I had to deliver a secret document,

00:14:22.470 --> 00:14:26.140
so I switched clothes with
Okuda Shouzaburou and went to Ako.

00:14:26.180 --> 00:14:27.140
What?

00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:28.810
Yomoshichi!

00:14:29.180 --> 00:14:30.430
Your face!

00:14:31.140 --> 00:14:32.430
How cruel!

00:14:33.980 --> 00:14:35.350
I got the wrong guy.

00:14:35.600 --> 00:14:38.900
Later, I heard Shouzaburou
went missing,

00:14:38.940 --> 00:14:40.610
and I was a little worried.

00:14:42.240 --> 00:14:46.490
By the way, what are you two
doing here together?

00:14:48.330 --> 00:14:49.700
A lot has happened.

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:53.210
In fact, Osode and I are now
a happily married couple.

00:14:53.290 --> 00:14:54.330
Wh-What?!

00:14:54.420 --> 00:14:55.540
That's crazy!

00:14:55.790 --> 00:14:57.330
Osode, tell me he's lying!

00:14:58.210 --> 00:14:59.920
I'm afraid it's true.

00:15:00.210 --> 00:15:03.010
We haven't broken off
our engagement!

00:15:03.220 --> 00:15:04.630
You're too late!

00:15:05.510 --> 00:15:09.430
Get over her.
Osode's my woman now.

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:12.100
You insolent bastard!
I won't forgive you!

00:15:12.220 --> 00:15:16.690
We made a promise that we have
to fulfill as husband and wife.

00:15:16.980 --> 00:15:18.020
Isn't that right, Osode?

00:15:20.400 --> 00:15:21.480
Osode.

00:15:21.530 --> 00:15:25.450
Which one of us do you choose?
Myself or Naosuke?

00:15:25.950 --> 00:15:27.780
Go on, Osode.
Tell him!

00:15:32.830 --> 00:15:36.670
Whatever happens,
I need you to trust me.

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:37.880
Yomoshichi,

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:40.000
I must talk to you.

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:43.380
Please come into the
back with me.

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:44.420
Right.

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:53.020
Damn it!

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:55.560
I'll just have to get him again!

00:16:14.370 --> 00:16:15.540
Now, now.

00:16:15.700 --> 00:16:17.370
Just be patient.

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:20.580
You're planning on siding
with Yomoshichi, aren't you?!

00:16:20.670 --> 00:16:22.130
What are you talking about?

00:16:22.380 --> 00:16:24.670
You and I are a real couple now.

00:16:24.710 --> 00:16:27.720
Until we've killed lemon,
I'll never leave your side.

00:16:31.640 --> 00:16:34.310
It's not convenient for me as well
having him here.

00:16:34.390 --> 00:16:36.060
Letting him live
can be troublesome.

00:16:36.770 --> 00:16:40.440
Then give Yomoshichi some
sake and get him drunk.

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:42.900
When I turn off the lantern,

00:16:42.940 --> 00:16:45.360
you appear from behind
the wooden panel.

00:16:46.360 --> 00:16:48.280
I'll quietly sneak up
and in one move...

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:54.740
Where's Naosuke?

00:16:56.040 --> 00:16:57.790
I sent him out
to buy some sake.

00:16:57.910 --> 00:16:58.910
I see.

00:16:59.290 --> 00:17:00.960
Then when he gets back here...

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:03.250
Don't underestimate Naosuke.

00:17:03.460 --> 00:17:05.590
I'll give him sake
and make sure he's drunk.

00:17:05.630 --> 00:17:06.670
Right.

00:17:06.840 --> 00:17:09.590
The signal is when the light
of the lantern goes out.

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:11.090
You appear through the panel.

00:17:11.180 --> 00:17:13.140
I'll strike him down in one move.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:15.390
I understand.

00:18:03.150 --> 00:18:04.100
Better be dead this time.

00:18:04.190 --> 00:18:05.190
What?!

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:06.520
Naosuke!

00:18:06.610 --> 00:18:07.360
You!

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:08.980
Then, who'd I just...?

00:18:10.650 --> 00:18:11.740
Osode!

00:18:12.950 --> 00:18:13.990
Osode!

00:18:16.910 --> 00:18:17.990
Osode!

00:18:18.330 --> 00:18:19.540
Osode!

00:18:19.660 --> 00:18:20.700
Why?!

00:18:20.790 --> 00:18:23.540
Why did it end up this way?!

00:18:24.710 --> 00:18:26.000
Yomoshichi,

00:18:26.340 --> 00:18:28.840
I'm very sorry.

00:18:29.380 --> 00:18:30.550
Naosuke,

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:33.720
carry out our promise.

00:18:34.470 --> 00:18:36.720
Get lemon.

00:18:45.600 --> 00:18:46.690
Osode!

00:18:47.690 --> 00:18:49.570
Osode!

00:18:53.740 --> 00:18:57.320
No. It can't be.
No way.

00:19:13.380 --> 00:19:14.420
Naosuke!

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:18.640
I'm a good-for-nothing lowlife.

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:28.190
I was the one
who killed Shouzaburou.

00:19:28.610 --> 00:19:30.570
I mistook him for you.

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:33.110
But none of that matters anymore.

00:19:33.530 --> 00:19:36.320
I realized that after reading
Osode's birth certificate.

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:40.870
Osode's real father
was Motomiya Sandayu,

00:19:40.910 --> 00:19:42.410
who's also my own father.

00:19:42.790 --> 00:19:47.540
Osode and I were blood siblings,
but were raised separately.

00:19:48.210 --> 00:19:52.920
I always wondered why a servant
like me would fall in love with her.

00:19:53.050 --> 00:19:55.800
Now I understand why.

00:19:58.260 --> 00:20:00.050
Yomoshichi,

00:20:00.470 --> 00:20:05.980
take my place and kill
Tamiya lemon for Osode.

00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:08.310
Get him.

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:31.250
Oiwa's sister, Osode,

00:20:31.290 --> 00:20:34.840
had chosen to end
her life in order

00:20:34.880 --> 00:20:37.800
to be released
from her cruel fate.

00:20:38.680 --> 00:20:42.800
Is destiny something that
cannot be controlled?

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:47.270
However, there is one man
in our story

00:20:47.350 --> 00:20:50.020
that continues to evade
the clutches of fate.

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:53.690
The curse of Oiwa has yet to end.

00:20:54.360 --> 00:20:58.900
The destiny that awaits lemon
is too terrifying to even repeat.

00:21:01.320 --> 00:21:04.530
The story will continue
in the next act.

